1
00:00:00,225 --> 00:00:07,275
This is The Vibe Coder's Handbook, a visual guide to commanding AI and modern developers.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,637
Apple doesn't sell websites.

3
00:00:09,637 --> 00:00:11,157
Nike doesn't sell buttons.

4
00:00:11,157 --> 00:00:12,735
Spotify doesn't sell menus.

5
00:00:12,735 --> 00:00:14,021
They sell experiences.

6
00:00:14,021 --> 00:00:17,470
The front end is the stage, where technology meets emotion.

7
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:23,667
The code is the machinery behind the curtain, and to build experiences, you must understand the machinery.

8
00:00:24,292 --> 00:00:25,497
Chapter one.

9
00:00:25,497 --> 00:00:28,208
How the web actually works.

10
00:00:28,933 --> 00:00:31,166
When you tap an app, it feels instant.

11
00:00:31,166 --> 00:00:35,337
But behind that single tap is a conversation between dozens of systems.

12
00:00:35,337 --> 00:00:44,796
Your request travels from the user, to the device, to the browser, across the internet, to a server, into a database, through code, and back again as a response.

13
00:00:44,796 --> 00:00:47,733
The Vibe Coder understands this invisible journey.

14
00:00:48,883 --> 00:00:50,618
The internet is three things.

15
00:00:50,618 --> 00:00:54,448
The client, the thing asking for information, like your browser.

16
00:00:54,448 --> 00:00:57,081
The server, the computer waiting to respond.

17
00:00:57,081 --> 00:01:00,013
And the network, the roads connecting everything.

18
00:01:00,013 --> 00:01:02,228
And no, the internet isn't the cloud.

19
00:01:02,228 --> 00:01:06,117
The cloud is just someone else's computer wearing a fancy jacket.

20
00:01:07,042 --> 00:01:08,720
A browser is a translator.

21
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:10,722
Humans see a beautiful website.

22
00:01:10,722 --> 00:01:13,433
The browser sees HTML, CSS and JavaScript.

23
00:01:13,433 --> 00:01:18,792
Its engine, Blink, WebKit or Gecko, takes raw code and turns it into an experience.

24
00:01:19,617 --> 00:01:21,580
Think of a website like property.

25
00:01:21,580 --> 00:01:27,768
The domain is the signpost, a human-friendly address, so you never have to remember a string of numbers.

26
00:01:27,768 --> 00:01:31,337
Hosting is the plot and the building, where your files live.

27
00:01:31,337 --> 00:01:33,717
And the website is the furniture inside.

28
00:01:34,692 --> 00:01:36,482
Hosting comes in three flavours.

29
00:01:36,482 --> 00:01:40,008
Shared hosting is an apartment building, great for small sites.

30
00:01:40,008 --> 00:01:43,308
A VPS is a townhouse, a private slice of a powerful server.

31
00:01:43,308 --> 00:01:47,113
Cloud hosting is a limitless hotel, built for apps and high traffic.

32
00:01:47,113 --> 00:01:51,142
Control the hosting, and you become the ecosystem, not just the builder.

33
00:01:52,117 --> 00:01:54,255
Every webpage stands on three layers.

34
00:01:54,255 --> 00:01:58,358
HTML is the skeleton, deciding what is a heading, an image or a button.

35
00:01:58,358 --> 00:02:01,998
CSS is the interior design: colours, spacing, fonts and layout.

36
00:02:01,998 --> 00:02:03,963
And JavaScript is the electricity.

37
00:02:03,963 --> 00:02:06,217
Without it, a website is just a poster.
